  "title": "4-Bit Subtractor (P - Q)",
  "description": "Design and implement a 4-bit Subtractor circuit that performs P - Q using 2's complement arithmetic (P + Q' + 1). P and Q are 4-bit numbers mapped to Switches 0-3 and Switches 4-7 respectively. Use one 7483 4-bit adder IC and XOR gates (7486 IC) to complement Q and provide the +1 Carry-In. Output LED C acts as an inverted-borrow indicator (C = 1 means P >= Q).",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "design",
